item.content:encoded:
It took a little longer than I would have liked, but I finally got around to updating the <a href="https://thomaslarock.com/rankings/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blogger Rankings</a>. A few people got moved around, and one got a warning. But the big news would be the unveiling of the Blogger Badges.

Yep, that's right, if you are listed on my Blogger Rankings page you should feel free to grab the appropriate badge and display on your blog. Why yes, you should feel special. And if you prefer, you can just use some HTML to point to the badge if you would rather do that instead.

So, here they are:
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_rdb1.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-2032" title="badge_rdb" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_rdb-169x200.jpg" alt="badge_rdb" /></a></p>
<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_rdb11.jpg">https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_rdb11.jpg</a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_mstr1.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-2029" title="badge_mstr" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_mstr-169x200.jpg" alt="badge_mstr" /></a></p>
<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_mstr11.jpg">https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_mstr11.jpg</a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_model1.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-2030" title="badge_model" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_model-169x200.jpg" alt="badge_model" /></a></p>
<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_model11.jpg">https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_model11.jpg</a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_msdb1.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-2028" title="badge_msdb" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_msdb-169x200.jpg" alt="badge_msdb" /></a></p>
<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_msdb11.jpg">https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_msdb11.jpg</a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_temp1.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-2031" title="badge_temp" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_temp-169x200.jpg" alt="badge_temp" /></a></p>
<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_temp11.jpg">https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/05/badge_temp11.jpg</a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Brent Ozar has already grabbed his badge and proudly displayed it on his blog. So, don't feel pressure to be like a master blogger such as Brent or anything...no sir, you make up your own mind.

Recently Brent Ozar decided to tell everyone about the ads he has been putting on his site. He and I had talked about it before his blog post, and I have had some ads on my site for about a week now. And, like Brent promised, I made four, check it out!

<a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/02/adsense_earnings21.png"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-904" title="adsense_earnings2" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/02/adsense_earnings21.png" alt="" /></a><a href="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/02/adsense_earnings11.png"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-903" title="adsense_earnings1" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/02/adsense_earnings11.png" alt="" /></a>

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Yep, that's right. Soon I will be sitting on a beach somewhere, all thanks to Google ads. Thanks Brent! By the time we meet again I should be able to buy you some candy, but that would cut deep into my retirement fund.

Speaking of which, I wonder if I could somehow set up a way to fund my <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">401k 301k 201k</span> 101k with adsense revenue. In fact, maybe everyone in America should start a blog, put Google ads on it, and use that in order to fund our Social Security accounts. That way we could have Google run our estate after we reach a certain age. They could build these cool retirement homes where the food is free and we surf the Intertubz all day and play Wii all night. And by doing so they would take the burden off the Federal government.

I think it is about time we see if Google is patriotic enough to do the right thing here. Call your local members of congress today and tell them that you want GoogleCare when you retire!

A while back I was sent this letter from a local car dealer. I remember reading it once, thinking something was wrong, and then doing a double-take when I read it a second time.

<img class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1163" title="fail001" src="https://thomaslarock.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/03/fail0011.jpg" alt="fail001" />

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Seriously, WTF?

I keep this letter on my cubical wall as a reminder to always check your work.

